  "premise_review": [
    "CrystalEndomorphism is an independent coherent typed-data component: preserve implicit C : CrystallineSite, explicit F : Crystal C, full map : ∀ X : C.Site.Obj, F.Section X → F.Section X and label : String. It assumes no heat flow or compatibility package and supplies no restriction/naturality/category law.",
    "The complete mixed HeatCompatibleEndomorphism record remains exact archive: preserve every C/F/H/e parameter, independent commutesWithHeat : Prop and its certified proof, and the actual dependent preservesHorizontal implication. No field is dropped or narrowed.",
    "preservesHorizontal is genuine typed content: for every original nabla : Connection F, X and section s, an already supplied horizontal proof for s is mapped to a horizontal proof for e.map X s. The exact theorem preserves E/nabla/X/s/h and applies E.preservesHorizontal nabla X s h; no premise is omitted.",
    "The Connection provider supplies horizontal as an arbitrary indexed predicate, without an equation tying it to Nabla, flatness or integrability. This is a real preservation-of-supplied-predicate implication, not a differential/analytic statement.",
    "commutesWithHeat is not a commutation equation between e.map and H.flow. Its theorem genuinely projects a supplied proof of that independent proposition. HeatFlowAction itself has actual Time/flow data but independent identity/semigroup propositions rather than defined action laws.",
    "The independent pointwise endomap is materialized whole as the actual seam before the mixed package. The mixed package and both complete proofs remain archival; extracting its local theorem would require a new original self-provider import absent from this source. The existing wrapper is reviewed separately with its original provider unchanged.",
    "Only outer namespace scaffolding and explicit Folder/CrystallineTensor opens are added around copied map data. Original import, complete source documentation, function/type/label bytes remain exact. No alias, provider substitution, heat compatibility, analytic heat flow, fixed-point existence or new geometric law is asserted."
  ],
